render('tink-town','Introducing Tink Town','A new business concept combining work, community and creative problem-solving. Human talent and emerging technology, brought together.',hero('Introducing Tink Town · In development','Bring the problem.<br>Let’s figure it out.','A new kind of place where talented people, powerful tools and everyday problems meet. A sister brand of River Tech, developed by River Tech LLC.',True,link('Visit the Tink Town website','https://tink.town/','button white'))+'''
<nav class="jump-nav" aria-label="Explore Tink Town"><div class="wrap"><a href="#concept">What we do</a><a href="dream-big.html">Dream Big ↗</a><a href="https://tink.town/community.html">Gatherings ↗</a><a href="https://tink.town/start.html?topic=general">Bring a project ↗</a></div></nav><section class="section" id="concept"><div class="wrap"><div class="intro-grid"><div><span class="eyebrow">The big idea</span><h2>Serious capability.<br>A welcoming place.</h2></div><div><p class="lead">Imagine a place where coffee and conversation sit alongside robotics, design, fabrication and creative work.</p><p>A business owner brings in a problem. A designer sketches an approach. Someone at the next table knows how to build it. A small conversation becomes a useful project.</p><p>Tink Town is being developed around that possibility: a place people want to spend time, and a business that helps them get things done.</p></div></div><figure class="concept-panorama" style="margin:48px 0 0"><img src="../assets/images/tink-town-concept.png" alt="Concept illustration of a café and workshop with people designing, building and collaborating"><figcaption class="small">Concept illustration. Tink Town is in development; this is not an existing facility.</figcaption></figure></div></section>
<section class="section tint-section"><div class="wrap"><span class="eyebrow">Three ways to belong</span><h2>Work here. Hang out here.<br>Bring us problems.</h2><div class="three-up"><article class="principle"><span class="number">01 / WORK HERE</span><h3>Put talent to work.</h3><p>The vision is a team combining AI, software, robotics and fabrication with design, storytelling, leadership and human judgment.</p></article><article class="principle"><span class="number">02 / HANG OUT HERE</span><h3>Let good things meet.</h3><p>Coffee, conversation, shared tools and creative work. A welcoming place where people can discover what others are making.</p></article><article class="principle"><span class="number">03 / BRING US PROBLEMS</span><h3>Make progress together.</h3><p>A practical starting point for a business, household or inventor with something to improve, automate, repair or create.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="wrap"><span class="eyebrow">What could that look like?</span><h2>Start with a real question.</h2>'''+tabs('possible-projects',['Make work simpler','Make something tangible','Make the story clear'],examplepanels)+'''</div></section>
<section class="section tink-next-paths"><div class="wrap"><span class="eyebrow">Find the details that matter to you</span><div class="journey-links"><a href="https://tink.town/#services">Projects, fabrication &amp; marketing ↗</a><a href="https://tink.town/learn.html">Training your team ↗</a><a href="dream-big.html">A place to belong: Dream Big ↗</a></div></div></section><section class="bridge-section"><div class="wrap bridge-inner"><div><span class="eyebrow">The River Tech connection</span><h2>From learning<br>to contribution.</h2></div><div><p>River Tech and Tink Town share a belief in human capability. We see opportunities to connect students and graduates with practical projects, experienced people and meaningful work.</p><p>School workshops, equipment access and career pathways are possibilities we are exploring with participating school operators.</p>'''+link('Explore the partnership vision','partnerships.html#schools')+'''</div></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="wrap intro-grid"><div><span class="eyebrow">The next chapter</span><h2>Start in Idaho.<br>Learn what can grow.</h2></div><div><p class="lead">The first Tink Town is intended to test the model: what people need, what creates value and what makes the place worth returning to.</p><p>We are interested in conversations with business owners, skilled collaborators, potential partners and investors who see the opportunity.</p><p class="inline-note">Tink Town is in development. Permanent premises, an opening date and a formal hiring program are still being developed. Visit the Tink Town website to explore services and discuss a project.</p></div></div></section>'''+cta('What would you bring to Tink Town?','Start a conversation','contact.html?topic=tink-town'))

render('partnerships','Partnerships','Explore partnerships with River Tech LLC for businesses, schools, churches and community groups. Practical contributions, shared opportunities and clear responsibilities.',hero('Partnerships','A useful relationship<br>starts with a shared need.','River Tech LLC welcomes businesses, schools, churches and community groups that want to connect capable people, useful technology and work that serves our region.')+'''
<nav class="jump-nav" aria-label="Partnership paths"><div class="wrap"><a href="#businesses">For businesses</a><a href="#schools">For schools</a><a href="#community">Church &amp; community</a><a href="#relationship">How it works</a></div></nav>
<section class="section" id="businesses"><div class="wrap intro-grid"><div><span class="eyebrow">For businesses</span><h2>Adapt with people<br>who can help.</h2></div><div><p class="lead">You do not need to predict every change. You need a way to turn the right changes into practical progress.</p><p>Talk with us about your challenges, your expertise and the opportunities you could bring to a partnership.</p><div class="list-rows"><article class="list-row"><h3>Bring a challenge</h3><p>Help shape the problems Tink Town is being developed to solve, from process improvement to prototypes and communication.</p></article><article class="list-row"><h3>Contribute expertise</h3><p>Explore projects, mentoring, equipment access or experiences that could benefit participating schools.</p></article><article class="list-row"><h3>Build a relationship</h3><p>Discuss appropriate recognition, promotion and offers alongside a clear contribution to students or the community.</p></article></div>'''+'''<div class="journey-links"><a href="https://tink.town/#services">See practical project examples ↗</a><a href="https://tink.town/learn.html">Explore team training ↗</a><a href="https://tink.town/talent.html">Explore hiring talent ↗</a></div>'''+link('Discuss a business partnership','contact.html?topic=business')+'''</div></div></section>
<section class="section tint-section" id="schools"><div class="wrap intro-grid"><div><span class="eyebrow">For schools</span><h2>Bring the wider world<br>into learning.</h2></div><div><p class="lead">Explore a relationship with Tink Town that connects education with people, equipment and practical work.</p><p>Potential activities include workshops, field trips, access to specialized technology and projects that give learning a real-world purpose.</p><p>Each school operator agrees to its own participation. Activities, student involvement and promotion are defined together.</p>'''+link('Discuss a school partnership','contact.html?topic=school-partnership')+'''</div></div></section>
<section class="bridge-section" id="community"><div class="wrap bridge-inner"><div><span class="eyebrow">Church &amp; community</span><h2>Rooted here.<br>Building together.</h2></div><div><p class="lead">Technology should strengthen the way of life we value.</p><p>We want to work alongside churches, farmers, hunters, hikers, craftspeople and the groups caring for North Idaho. Bring your experience, a local need or an idea for something we could accomplish together.</p>'''+link('Explore church and community partnerships','community.html')+'''</div></div></section>
<section class="section" id="relationship"><div class="wrap"><span class="eyebrow">The starting point</span><h2>Agree on what each<br>partner brings.</h2><ol class="steps"><li><h3>Find the common purpose</h3><p>Start with the people you want to serve and the problem or opportunity you share.</p></li><li><h3>Shape a useful exchange</h3><p>Define contributions, activities, recognition and any fees or equipment arrangements.</p></li><li><h3>Make responsibilities clear</h3><p>Identify the participating organizations and agree on what each can deliver.</p></li></ol><p class="inline-note">This partnership model is being developed. No standard membership fee or automatic access to schools is offered.</p></div></section>'''+cta('What could we accomplish together?','Talk about a partnership','contact.html?topic=business'))

render('dream-big','Dream Big','Find your people and take the next step with River Tech and Tink Town.',hero('Dream Big · Part of the Tink Town launch plan','Dream big.<br>You’ve found your people.','Maybe you have an idea that won’t leave you alone. Maybe you sense God has given you something to contribute, but you haven’t quite found its shape—or the people to build it with.',True,link('Bring your idea','contact.html?topic=dream-big','button white'))+'''<nav class="jump-nav" aria-label="Explore Dream Big"><div class="wrap"><a href="tink-town.html">← Tink Town</a><a href="#belong">A place to belong</a><a href="#next-step">Your next step</a></div></nav><section class="section" id="belong"><div class="wrap intro-grid"><div><span class="eyebrow">You don’t have to figure it out alone</span><h2>A place to belong.<br>People to build with.</h2></div><div><p class="lead">We will offer a welcoming place to hang out, weekly gatherings where friendships grow and ideas take shape, and affordable purpose coaching to help you discover your gifts and put them to work.</p><p>Come for coffee and conversation. Bring the idea you can’t shake—or the questions you haven’t figured out yet. Find encouragement, discover your gifts and take practical steps toward the work God is calling you to do.</p><p class="inline-note">Part of the Tink Town launch plan. The location, gathering schedule and coaching arrangements are being developed.</p></div></div></section><section class="section tint-section" id="next-step"><div class="wrap"><span class="eyebrow">Fan your calling into flame</span><h2>Start where you are.</h2><div class="three-up"><article class="principle"><span class="number">01 / BELONG</span><h3>Find your people.</h3><p>A table to gather around, friends to think with and a community that wants to see you grow.</p></article><article class="principle"><span class="number">02 / DISCOVER</span><h3>Explore your purpose.</h3><p>What are you good at? What matters deeply to you? Who could you serve? Practical coaching helps turn those questions into direction.</p></article><article class="principle"><span class="number">03 / BUILD</span><h3>Take the next step.</h3><p>Try an idea, learn a skill, find a collaborator or begin a project. You don’t need every answer before you start.</p></article></div></div></section>'''+cta('What might God be calling you to build?','Let’s talk about it','contact.html?topic=dream-big'))

render('community','Church & Community','Church and community partnerships rooted in Christian faith, Idaho values and useful work for North Idaho.',hero('Church & community','Rooted in what matters.<br>Ready for what comes next.','Christian faith, the natural world and useful technology belong together in the future we are building. Innovation should serve family, church, community and country.',True,link('Find a way to work together','#together','button white'))+'''
<nav class="jump-nav" aria-label="Church and community partnerships"><div class="wrap"><a href="#churches">For churches</a><a href="#colleges">For colleges</a><a href="#community-groups">For community groups</a><a href="#together">Start together</a></div></nav>
<section class="section"><div class="wrap intro-grid"><div><span class="eyebrow">The future belongs here</span><h2>Moving forward.<br>Staying grounded.</h2></div><div><p class="lead">We want to help our community move forward without leaving behind what makes it worth belonging to.</p><p>Faith, time outdoors, craftsmanship, grit and care for our neighbors belong in the future we are building. River Tech develops problem-solvers. Tink Town puts problem-solvers to work. Both should strengthen the people and places around them.</p><p>That begins with listening to those who already serve this region—and finding useful work to do together.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="section tint-section" id="churches"><div class="wrap intro-grid"><div><span class="eyebrow">Church partners</span><h2>Shared faith.<br>Practical service.</h2></div><div><p class="lead">Churches exalt Jesus, bring people together, care for families and give the next generation a foundation. We share that calling and want to support it through practical service and partnership.</p><div class="list-rows"><article class="list-row"><h3>Equip young people</h3><p>Explore workshops where youth can learn design, robotics or practical AI skills—and use them on a project that serves someone.</p></article><article class="list-row"><h3>Serve together</h3><p>Bring a community need: a useful item to design, materials for an outreach project, or a task that skilled volunteers and emerging makers could tackle together.</p></article><article class="list-row"><h3>Gather in worship</h3><p>River Tech is also a Christian performing arts school. Our music and performance experience equips us to help lead worship, alongside prayer, devotionals and Christian talks, in gatherings shaped together with church partners.</p></article><article class="list-row"><h3>Bring faith and learning together</h3><p>Imagine a youth workshop that pairs robotics with a devotional, or a team evening combining practical AI training, dinner, prayer and worship. Learn to use technology ethically and safely: protect people’s privacy, check what AI produces, communicate truthfully and keep human judgment central. The purpose is to glorify God, serve others and share the good news of Jesus.</p></article><article class="list-row"><h3>Support your ministry</h3><p>Discuss websites, videos, printed materials or simpler administrative workflows that help your team spend more time serving people.</p></article></div>'''+link('Talk about a church partnership','contact.html?topic=church')+'''</div></div></section>
<section class="section" id="colleges"><div class="wrap intro-grid"><div><span class="eyebrow">College partners</span><h2>Your students.<br>A new set of tools.</h2></div><div><p class="lead">A Bible college brings its students, mission and theological setting. River Tech can work with its team to develop practical technology teaching grounded in Christian faith.</p><p>Start with a guest workshop, a short course or a course module. Together, we can shape the content around what students need to do in ministry and working life.</p><div class="list-rows"><article class="list-row"><h3>AI for ministry</h3><p>Research, communications, administration and practical AI workflows—with Christian ethics, discernment and safe use at the center. Learn to protect confidential information, check AI-generated material and communicate truthfully while using technology to serve people and share the gospel.</p></article><article class="list-row"><h3>Creative technology</h3><p>Video, websites, graphic design and printed materials. Students could finish with something useful for a church or ministry, such as a website, outreach campaign or improved administrative process.</p></article><article class="list-row"><h3>Faith and emerging technology</h3><p>Explore human dignity, work, service and stewardship alongside hands-on experience with the tools changing our world. Consider how to use technology in ways that glorify God, strengthen human relationships and support the church’s mission.</p></article></div><p>We would agree on learning goals, instructors, delivery and cost with the college. The college determines whether and how the course counts toward its qualifications.</p>'''+link('Explore a college partnership','contact.html?topic=college')+'''</div></div></section>
<section class="section" id="community-groups"><div class="wrap intro-grid"><div><span class="eyebrow">Community partners</span><h2>Local knowledge.<br>New possibilities.</h2></div><div><p class="lead">Farmers, hunters, hikers, craftspeople and outdoor groups understand needs that technology alone cannot identify. That experience belongs at the table.</p><div class="list-rows"><article class="list-row"><h3>Bring a real problem</h3><p>A farm needs a custom bracket. An outdoor group needs trail signs. A local maker needs a prototype or a clearer way to reach customers. Start with what would actually help.</p></article><article class="list-row"><h3>Share what you know</h3><p>Explore demonstrations, mentoring and workshops connecting practical technology with agriculture, outdoor life, repair and craftsmanship.</p></article><article class="list-row"><h3>Care for this place</h3><p>Consider a service project, educational event or useful tool that helps people enjoy and care for our land and community.</p></article></div>'''+link('Bring a community idea','contact.html?topic=community')+'''</div></div></section>
<section class="bridge-section" id="together"><div class="wrap bridge-inner"><div><span class="eyebrow">Start with one useful thing</span><h2>A relationship built<br>around shared work.</h2></div><div><p>Tell us who you serve, what you know and one thing you would like to make possible. Together, we can define a first project, the people involved and what each side can contribute.</p><p>Contributions might include expertise, volunteer time, materials, space or paid project work. We agree on any costs and responsibilities for each activity; there is no standard paid membership requirement.</p><p class="small">These are invitations to help shape the work. Tink Town is in development; activities involving a school require that school operator’s agreement.</p></div></div></section>'''+cta('What could we do for our community?','Start a conversation','contact.html?topic=community'))

render('investing','Build with us — investing and partnership','Seven practical ways to help build River Tech and Tink Town in North Idaho.',hero('Investing & partnership','Big ideas.<br>Close to home.','We love following SpaceX, Nvidia and the wider market. But imagine seeing your investment help local talent flourish, local businesses adapt and good ideas become useful work—right here where you live.',True,link('Explore the seven opportunities','#opportunities','button white'))+build_opportunity_hub(link)+'''
<section class="bridge-section"><div class="wrap bridge-inner"><div><span class="eyebrow">A shared starting point</span><h2>Clear expectations.<br>A useful relationship.</h2></div><div><p>The River Tech concept is in practice in Post Falls. Tink Town’s location, services and operating arrangements are still being developed.</p><p>Each opportunity begins with a conversation about fit, responsibilities and what both sides need. Any financial terms require a separate written agreement; the 6% lending rate is a working proposal.</p><p class="small" style="margin-top:20px">This page invites exploratory conversations. It does not offer securities or set investment terms.</p></div></div></section>'''+cta('Not sure where you fit? Let’s talk.','Start a conversation','contact.html'))

render('story','Our story','Dan and Mary Hegelund are developing River Tech and Tink Town, rooted in Christian faith, Idaho community and practical enterprise.',hero('Our story','A school was<br>the beginning.','Dan and Mary Hegelund’s work in education, music and community led to River Tech. Tink Town asks where that same belief in people can go next.')+'''
<section class="section"><div class="wrap brand-feature"><div><span class="eyebrow">The founders</span><h2>Dan & Mary<br>Hegelund</h2><p class="lead" style="margin-top:25px">Educators, creators and builders with a shared Christian faith and a home in Post Falls, Idaho.</p><p style="margin-top:18px">Their work brings together a conviction that education should develop the whole person and that people should have meaningful ways to put their abilities to use.</p></div><figure style="margin:0"><div class="photo"><img src="../assets/images/teachers/dan-mary-hegelund.jpg" alt="Dan and Mary Hegelund, founders of River Tech LLC"></div><figcaption class="caption">Dan and Mary Hegelund</figcaption></figure></div></section>
<section class="section tint-section"><div class="wrap"><span class="eyebrow">The thread through it all</span><p class="story-quote">People are capable of more when they have something worth learning, something worth making and a community to build with.</p></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="wrap"><span class="eyebrow">How the idea grew</span><h2>From education<br>to enterprise.</h2><div class="timeline"><article class="timeline-item"><time>2009</time><div><h3>The original school proposal</h3><p>While living in Sweden, Dan wrote a proposal for a Christian school bringing performing arts, technology and academics together.</p></div></article><article class="timeline-item"><time>2021</time><div><h3>River Tech in practice</h3><p>The River Tech program opened in Post Falls, Idaho, turning the educational idea into a school community.</p></div></article><article class="timeline-item"><time>2026</time><div><h3>A home for the concepts</h3><p>River Tech LLC provides a dedicated home for the school brand and concept, separate from individual school operators.</p></div></article><article class="timeline-item"><time>The next chapter</time><div><h3>Introducing Tink Town</h3><p>A business concept built around skilled people, useful technology and a welcoming place to work on real problems.</p></div></article></div></div></section>
<section class="culture-statement" aria-labelledby="culture-title"><div class="wrap"><span class="eyebrow">What we stand for</span><h2 id="culture-title">Christian faith. Idaho roots.</h2><p>Our work is grounded in Christian faith and the Idaho values of family, church, community, hard work, patriotism and personal responsibility. We believe in merit, grit and entrepreneurship: developing our gifts, meeting difficult challenges and building things that serve others. We value truth, human dignity and honest discussion. Technology should strengthen real life, never replace family, friendship, faith or time outdoors. These convictions shape how we teach, how we do business and the partnerships we choose.</p></div></section>'''+cta('Help shape the next chapter.','Start a conversation','contact.html'))

render('contact','Start a conversation','Contact River Tech LLC about business partnerships, operating a school, Tink Town or potential investment.',hero('Start a conversation','What do you<br>want to build?','Tell us what you are working on, what you see changing and where you think we might be able to work together.')+'''
<section class="section"><div class="wrap contact-grid"><div><form id="inquiry-form"><div class="form-row"><div class="field"><label for="name">Your name</label><input id="name" name="name" autocomplete="name" required maxlength="150"></div><div class="field"><label for="email">Your email</label><input id="email" name="email" type="email" autocomplete="email" required maxlength="254"></div></div><div class="field"><label for="organization">Business or organization (optional)</label><input id="organization" name="organization" autocomplete="organization" maxlength="200"></div><div class="field"><label for="topic">I would like to talk about</label><select id="topic" name="topic"><option value="business">A business partnership</option><option value="school">Operating a River Tech school</option><option value="school-partnership">A school partnership</option><option value="church">A church partnership</option><option value="college">A college course partnership</option><option value="community">A community partnership</option><option value="tink-town">Tink Town</option><option value="dream-big">Dream Big and purpose coaching</option><option value="investing">Exploring investment</option><option value="property">Providing a property</option><option value="equipment">Providing equipment</option><option value="lending">Lending capital</option><option value="projects">Bringing a project</option><option value="hiring">Hiring talent</option><option value="training">Training a team</option><option value="events">Hosting an event</option><option value="general">Something else</option></select></div><div class="field"><label for="message">What do you have in mind?</label><textarea id="message" name="message" required maxlength="6000" placeholder="A little about you, your idea or the problem you are thinking about."></textarea></div><button class="button" type="submit">Prepare an email <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button><p class="form-help">This prepares a draft in your email app. Nothing is sent through this website.</p></form><div class="email-ready" id="email-ready" hidden><h3 id="email-ready-title" tabindex="-1">Your message is ready.</h3><p>Open the draft, review it in your email app, then send it when you are ready.</p><a class="button" id="email-open" href="mailto:hello@rivertech.llc">Open email draft ↗</a> <button class="button secondary" type="button" id="copy-message">Copy message</button><p class="copy-note" id="copy-note" role="status"></p></div></div><aside class="contact-aside"><div class="aside-block"><span class="eyebrow">Direct contact</span><h3>A conversation<br>with the founders.</h3><p><a href="mailto:hello@rivertech.llc">hello@rivertech.llc</a></p><p>Dan & Mary Hegelund<br>River Tech LLC<br>Post Falls, Idaho</p></div><div class="aside-block"><h3>Looking for the school?</h3><p>For enrollment, tours, tuition and family information, contact the individual school.</p>'''+link('Visit the Post Falls school','https://rivertechschool.com')+'''</div></aside></div></section>''')

